# Trains (Conductor ritual)

## Roles

- **Conductor** — one per game day; lock spawns empty train (5×6 cargo slots).
- **VIP** — boards after lock/spawn; VIP chooses 2 of 4 rider cars. HQ VIP assign/spin requires `lockedAt`.
- **Guardian** — defends on plunder: VIP squads if `guardianIsVip`, else Conductor.
- **Lock** — `lockedAt` spawns the train and freezes the conductor pick; VIP may still be set afterward (unlock/override = exceptional + audited).

**Lifecycle order:** assign conductor → **lock** → assign VIP. Guided Simple Mode follows the same order. Product UX invariants (day vs week paint, swap dates, share preview, wizard recovery): [trains-conductor-ux.mdc](./trains-conductor-ux.mdc).

## Week templates

| Template | Typical use |
|----------|-------------|
| `vs_push_week` | **Composite:** Tue–Sat `vs_push_weekdays` + Sun–Mon `r4_event_vip` |
| `vs_push_weekdays` | Mon `donations_top`; Tue/Fri `vs_high_score`; Wed/Thu/Sat `vs_top_10` |
| `top_vs` / `top_vr` | Paint-only segments — `vs_top_n` / `vr_top_n` with `conductor_config.topN` |
| `r4_event_vip` | Segment — `r4_sequence` conductor + `event_top_x_lottery` VIP (silvery cell) |
| `economy_week` / `r3_recognition` | R3 lottery all days when saving inventory |
| `price_is_right` | R3 lottery most days with optional **ticket weighting**; **Saturday** = heavy-hitter lottery among max-ticket overrides |
| `r4_train_week` | Officer sequence all days |
| `donations_week` | Top donor / second donor |
| `custom` | Placeholder for officer-defined days |

Templates expand to **per-day** `train_day_configs` (conductor + VIP mechanisms).

**Composite templates** (`COMPOSITE_WEEK_TEMPLATES` in `src/lib/trains/week-template-registry.shared.ts`) map a whole-week preset to segment templates per **calendar DOW relative to Tuesday** (Tue=0 … Mon=6 via `compositeSegmentDayIndex` in `src/lib/trains/week-template-registry.shared.ts`) — independent of alliance `trainWeekStartDow`. Segment paint is stored on each day's `conductorConfig.paintTemplate`. User-defined reusable composites can extend the same registry later.

**`takedown_week`** — composite Saturday segment for Price Is Freight heavy-hitter (max-ticket list). Conductor rolls use the **with-replacement** PIF path (`usesPriceIsFreightConductorRoll` in `src/lib/trains/heavy-hitter-pool.shared.ts`), not depleting `heavy_hitter` pool consumption.

## Economy-week pivot (per-day overrides)

When VS Day 1 looks unwinnable, officers **paint Tue–Sun** with `economy_week` (or similar) without replacing the whole week.

- **`train_day_configs.is_override = 1`** when an officer paints a day with a template different from the week baseline.
- **`train_week_schedules.is_pivot = 1`** when Tue+ economy overrides apply during a `vs_push_week` baseline.
- **Pivot window:** Mon 22:00 – Tue 12:00 server time (UTC−2).

Do **not** use whole-week `setWeekTemplate` for pivot — it clears overrides.

## Scheduling UX (product direction)

- Officers plan on a **calendar** with template palette + per-day paint (Phase B).
- **Day vs week paint are exclusive:** single-day paint / long-press / guided “Change pick” use `DAY_PAINT_TEMPLATES` (no composites). Whole-week or multi-day paint uses week/composite templates. Details: [trains-conductor-ux.mdc](./trains-conductor-ux.mdc).
- **Week strip:** every tile always shows conductor name or "—". Long-press or right-click → day-mechanism menu (`DAY_PAINT_TEMPLATES`) → `paintDates([date], template)`. Tap still selects the day. Week-template control stays separate (composites OK).
- When the roster has members (`activeMemberCount > 0`), show **preview** day configs from the anchor template — never a blank “create week” gate. Missing week template must **not** block the guided day funnel.
- Persist `train_week_schedules` on the **first officer schedule mutation** (paint, template change, lock) via `ensureWeekScheduleBaseline` — not on page load.
- **Clear week schedule** (`DELETE /api/trains/schedule`) is **pre-production only** (`isDevOrPreviewEnvironment`): train managers (`trains:write`) may discard a persisted week back to draft preview. Hidden and 404-gated in production. Does **not** delete conductor records.
- Do **not** show schedulable train UI when **`activeMemberCount === 0`** (native alliances need roster first).
- **Game season** is managed under **Settings**, not on the trains page.
- **Dates** — eligibility and “today” use game server calendar (`game-time`, UTC−2). Monday never requires prior-day VS; Sunday prior-day VS = Saturday.
- **Swap / make-up** — future unlocked days only; next-3 quick picks may cross weeks + date picker (`conductor-swap.shared.ts`). Moves drafts only — does not lock. Re-stamps depleting-pool `selectedForDate` onto the new days.
- **Spin for the week** — rolls remaining wheel days as drafts; does not lock.
- **Unlock** — undoes spawn/`lockedAt` only; does **not** return the conductor to a depleting pool. Clearing the assignment or re-rolling releases the pool slot.
- **History import** (`/trains/history-import`, `trains:write`) — paste newest→oldest conductors (optional date anchors or newest-date picker; oldest inferred from list length), review matches, batch-lock **past** days. Include **former/inactive** roster members in match + picker (label inactive; status “Matched to an inactive member”; still commitable). Prefer active when both would match. Unmatched rows are **skipped** on commit so partial history can ship. Date gaps: flag row, re-base timeline, allow blank placeholder days before the flagged row (unknown conductors; not imported). Same locked conductor = skip; different locked = conflict (no overwrite). No Discord announce. **Does not mutate depleting pools** — import has no reliable historical mechanism (VS Push / event Top N vs Economy Week / R3 lottery), so pool depletion must stay on live roll/lock paths. Video rematch must **not** auto-include former. Shared parse: `conductor-history-import.shared.ts`; API: `POST/GET /api/trains/conductor/history-import`.
- **Simple vs advanced mode** — guided stepper (default) vs quick-actions layout; parity contract in [trains-simple-advanced-modes.mdc](./trains-simple-advanced-modes.mdc).

## Pools

- `r3_lottery` → `r3` pool; `heavy_hitter_lottery` → `heavy_hitter` pool; `r4_sequence` → `r4_plus`.
- Selected members are removed from the current generation (`selectedAt` / `selectedForDate`).
- **`train_conductor_records`** — permanent alliance audit of conductor + VIP per date. Names are **denormalized** at assign/import time.
- **History display vs churn** — History UI/API must render those denormalized conductor/VIP/guardian snapshots — **never** blank a past Conductor/VIP solely because the member later left (`former`). Do not join history reads to the active-only roster for display names. Import of former members must still write the denormalized name.
- **Active-only eligibility** — Conductor and VIP **rolls** may only select members with roster status **not** `former` (and still on the alliance roster). Seed/reseed already use `listActiveAllianceMembersForPool`. Mid-generation: filter and **prune unselected** `conductor_pool_entries` for members who become `former` (at roll/pick time and when roster sync marks former). Do not erase already-selected slots in a generation. Incomplete history beats empty history; leavers must not stay in live Conductor/VIP pools.
- **Manual conductor pick vs the wheel** — Eligibility (current pool generation, rank band, VS/donation minimums) is a **hard** requirement for the spin wheel. Officers may assign **any active** alliance member as conductor via Pick Conductor after confirming an eligibility override. Do not 400-block a manual pick of an active member. Overriding does **not** insert a spent or missing member back onto the wheel's eligibility side.

### Pool rank (R3 / R4+ eligibility)

`resolveMemberPoolAllianceRank` in `rank-history.ts`: **prefer HQ rank events** when present (`member_alliance_rank_events`); do **not** take `Math.max(event, synced)` — a stale higher Ashed-synced rank must not override a confirmed HQ demotion. Use synced roster / `ashedRankRaw` only when no HQ event exists yet.

**Current-generation rank sync** (`planCurrentGenerationRankEligibilitySync` / `syncRankEligibilityForCurrentGenerations`): on member rank dual-write, roster sync/commit, and when reading the current `r3` / `r4_plus` generation, drop **unselected** rows that are no longer rank-eligible (R3→R2, R3→R4, R4→R3) and insert currently eligible active members who are missing from that generation (e.g. a new R4 account). Do **not** re-add a member who already has a **selected** row in that generation — thrash between R3 and R4 must not refresh eligibility inside one rotation. Do not seed a generation that does not exist yet, and do not reopen a fully selected generation (the next seed includes current ranks). Do not erase selected history. Heavy-hitter / event Top X pools are unchanged.

### Conductor minimums (VS / donation settings)

Alliance settings may require minimum **VS** (and donation, when HQ stores donation scores) for **Price Is Freight** paints only (`price_is_right`, `price_is_right_weekdays`, `takedown_week`) via `conductorMinimumsApplyForPaintTemplate` → `usesPriceIsFreightConductorRoll`. Economy Week and other depleting-pool paints spin the rank pool without those floors. Enforcement uses **Ashed daily VS** summed over the evaluation window (prior calendar day or prior train week) — **not** season VR. Do not gate minimum checks on `classifyVsDataNeed` / guided `prerequisites`; missing VS rows count as zero. R4+ pools ignore minimums.

### Price Is Freight (`price_is_right`)

TPIF conductor rolls are **with-replacement** daily draws (`rollPriceIsFreightConductor`). They do **not** seed, mark, or reseed `conductor_pool_entries`. The same member may win consecutive days. Non-TPIF `r3_lottery` / `heavy_hitter_lottery` (e.g. `economy_week`, `r3_recognition`) still use depleting pools. **`takedown_week`** (composite Saturday segment) uses the same with-replacement PIF conductor path as weekday `price_is_right` / `price_is_right_weekdays` — gate via `usesPriceIsFreightConductorRoll` in `src/lib/trains/heavy-hitter-pool.shared.ts` (not `isPriceIsRightPaintTemplate` alone, which excludes `takedown_week`).

Two alliance-configurable modes (settings → **The Price Is Freight**):

| Mode | Eligibility | Draw |
|------|-------------|------|
| **Legacy band** (`weightingEnabled = 0`) | Prior-day VS in `[7.2M, threshold + fudge%]` when threshold set (**takedown overrides stay eligible above the band**); **null threshold = no VS filter** (equal odds among R3) | Uniform random among live eligible set |
| **Ticket weighting** (`weightingEnabled = 1`) | R3 with `ticketCount > 0` | Weighted random by tickets |

New alliances default `train_economy_threshold_points` to **8,500,000** (`PRICE_IS_RIGHT_DEFAULT_ECONOMY_THRESHOLD_POINTS`). Officers may clear it to disable VS filtering.

**Saturday** draws uniformly among members in `train_price_is_right_max_ticket_member_ids` (also with-replacement). Settings updates may still sync a legacy `heavy_hitter` pool row for non-TPIF use, but TPIF Saturday rolls do not consume it.

**Ticket weighting rules:**

- Floor: prior-day VS ≥ **7,200,000** for any tickets.
- Sweet spot near 7.2M → max tickets (1024); exponential decay upward.
- **Cliff** (`train_economy_threshold_points`): decay scale; defaults to **9M** when unset.
- **Hard cutoff** (optional): VS > cliff → 0 tickets; fudge % ignored.
- **Takedown / heavy-hitter override** (`train_price_is_right_max_ticket_member_ids`): listed members always get max tickets on weekday raffles; Saturday lottery is drawn only from this list.
- Member-visible **odds panel** on `/trains` for **every** TPIF day (`GET /api/trains/price-is-right/tickets`): `mode` = `weighted` \| `uniform` \| `heavy_hitter` (equal `1/N` when not weighted).
- **Prior-day VS podium** on all `price_is_right` days (`GET /api/trains/price-is-right/leaderboard`): ranks R3 members with prior-day VS ≥ 7.2M by distance above 7.2M (not VR). Discord announcement fires after **vs-performance** video submit when the next train day is PIF (`announcePriceIsRightLeaderboardAfterVsUpload`); manual/worker trigger at `/api/internal/train/price-is-right-leaderboard` (not cron-scheduled).

Schema: `train_price_is_right_*` on `alliances`.

## RBAC

| Action | Permission |
|--------|------------|
| Read dashboard, schedule, history | `scores:read` |
| Roll, lock, schedule paint, pool reseed | `trains:write` via `requireTrainOfficer` |

All queries filter by session **`allianceId`**.

## Top VS / Top VR scopes

| Surface | Mechanism | Scopes | Score source | Template-time lock |
|--------|-----------|--------|--------------|--------------------|
| **Top VS** | `vs_top_n` (+ legacy `vs_high_score`→1, `vs_top_10`→10) | 1, 3, 5, 10 | Prior-day **daily** Ashed VS (active roster only) | **Never** by reporter/score count — spin gated by `prior_day_vs` upload readiness |
| **Top VR** | `vr_top_n` | 3, 5, 10 only | Season HQ VR (active roster only) | Scope N locked until active-roster `vrReporterCount >= 2×N` |

Paint ids `top_vs` / `top_vr` open a scope picker. `conductor_config.topN` is merged with `paintTemplate` (do not wipe `topN` in `withPaintTemplateConfig`).

## Data sources

- **Top VS** (`vs_high_score` / `vs_top_10` / `vs_top_n`) — prior-day **daily** Ashed `VSScore` for T−1 (`vsScoreReferenceDate(trainDate)`); filter out `is_weekly` week-ending rows; **dedupe by member** (keep max score) before Top N slice; **intersect with active HQ roster** (exclude former members). Empty when T−1 is Sunday (VS break). Readiness `prior_day_vs`.
- **Top VR** (`vr_top_n`) — HQ `memberSeasonVr` among active roster members; readiness kind `vr`.
- **Event Top X VIP** — HQ season VR / event scores.
- **Pools, economy filters, Price Is Right tickets** — HQ roster + prior-day VS where applicable.
- Donation wheels require manual officer picks until HQ stores donation scores.
- Do not show schedule preview before roster import (`activeMemberCount === 0`).
